    "title": "Remove Duplicate Pending Transactions by ID",
    "prompt": "You are maintaining a fintech application's `transaction_queue` table that stores pending payment requests. Due to a system bug, some transactions were submitted multiple times with identical `user_id`, `merchant_id`, and `amount` but different `queue_id` values. Write a single DELETE statement that removes all duplicate rows within each (`user_id`, `merchant_id`, `amount`) group, keeping only the row with the smallest `queue_id` (the earliest submission). After the DELETE, select all remaining rows ordered by `queue_id` ascending to confirm the cleanup.",
